 "_doc": "Keyword routes for skill_router.py. Order = priority; at most max_hits routes are named per prompt. 'any' and 'not' are regexes compiled with re.I | re.ASCII, so \\b only marks ASCII word edges (CJK next to an acronym still counts as a boundary, e.g. 用MODIS). Matching skips <pasted_content> blocks and forked-session Background/Task preambles. Prefer two-part patterns (verb + noun) over bare nouns: routed skills are 3-61 KB and some open with approval gates. Edit here, then run test_skill_router.py and replay_skill_router.py. This is an EXAMPLE: copy it to ~/.claude/hooks/skill_routes.json and edit the routes to your own skills and habits.",
